@meeting train.m7.halloran-emeka
// Pillar 5, M7 (Day 5, Friday): the main Day 5 version. Emeka Halloran (Works systems officer, he/him) teaches the
// scanner at the board; Torres is off on Fridays and left his old scanner with a note. Head writer, seat W.
title: Torres's old scanner
from: Emeka Halloran
gist: Emeka gave you Torres's old scanner. It reads a machine's parts, so you can choose which one to fetch.
== lines
halloran-emeka: Morning, morning. Have you eaten? Good. Zeke left you a present.   [gesture]
halloran-emeka > you: His old scanner. With a note. He made me promise not to read it. I read it.   [laugh]
halloran-emeka: Hold it to a panel and it reads every part. A bar and a word each.
halloran-emeka: Good, worn, low, failing. Usually one's clearly off, and that's the part you fetch.
halloran-emeka: Now and then two read low. Then you trust your eyes. What's the card say? What do you see?
halloran-emeka: Pick the wrong one and you walk back. That's all. I've walked back more than anyone.
? choice
* Two low parts. How do I choose?   rel:halloran-emeka+2 flavour:practical
  halloran-emeka: Look before you scan. Cool by the door is a seal. Cool all over, the element. Lovely.   [nod]
* Zeke gave me his scanner?   rel:halloran-emeka+1 flavour:listen
  halloran-emeka: He did. He'll say it was nothing. It wasn't. He's had it since his first week.
* (Weigh it in your hand)
  halloran-emeka: Older than you, he says. Still works, though. Like me. Mostly.   [laugh]
halloran-emeka: Right. One's held for us. I'll read the first, you watch. Then the next is all yours.
